\# GCE Performance Rules

\#\# Purpose

This rule governs every performance-related implementation across the GCE platform.

Whenever creating or modifying:

\- Pages  
\- Components  
\- APIs  
\- Database Queries  
\- Dashboards  
\- Authentication  
\- Marketplace  
\- AI Features  
\- Payments  
\- Infrastructure

always follow the official performance documentation before writing code.

\---

\# Documentation Priority

Always consult:

\`\`\`  
32\_Performance\_Optimization\_Expert.md  
\`\`\`

This document is the single source of truth for performance optimization.

\---

\# Performance Philosophy

Every feature should be:

\- Fast  
\- Efficient  
\- Scalable  
\- Responsive  
\- Lightweight  
\- Production Ready

Performance is a core feature of the platform.

Never optimize only after development.

Performance should be considered while writing code.

\---

\# Frontend Performance

Always:

\- Minimize re-renders  
\- Lazy load heavy components  
\- Use dynamic imports  
\- Optimize images  
\- Reduce bundle size  
\- Use memoization where appropriate  
\- Keep components small

Avoid unnecessary rendering.

\---

\# React Best Practices

Prefer:

\- React.memo()  
\- useMemo()  
\- useCallback()

only when they provide measurable benefits.

Do not overuse memoization.

\---

\# Component Design

Components should:

\- Have one responsibility  
\- Be reusable  
\- Be lightweight  
\- Receive only required props

Avoid giant components.

\---

\# Motion Performance

Whenever using Motion:

Follow:

\`\`\`  
27\_Frontend\_Animations.md  
\`\`\`

Animations should:

\- Use transforms  
\- Use opacity  
\- Avoid layout thrashing  
\- Respect reduced motion settings

Never create expensive animations.

\---

\# Next.js Optimization

Always prefer:

\- Server Components  
\- Dynamic Imports  
\- Image Optimization  
\- Streaming  
\- Static Rendering where appropriate

Avoid unnecessary Client Components.

\---

\# API Performance

APIs should:

\- Return only required fields  
\- Avoid duplicate queries  
\- Minimize processing time  
\- Be properly indexed

Avoid excessive payloads.

\---

\# Database Performance

Always:

\- Use indexes  
\- Optimize joins  
\- Paginate large datasets  
\- Select only required columns

Avoid:

\- SELECT \*  
\- N+1 Queries  
\- Duplicate database requests

\---

\# Query Optimization

Every query should:

\- Be efficient  
\- Be reusable  
\- Be indexed where necessary

Avoid unnecessary nested queries.

\---

\# Caching

Whenever appropriate:

Use:

\- Browser Cache  
\- Server Cache  
\- CDN Cache  
\- API Cache

Cache frequently accessed data.

Never cache sensitive information.

\---

\# Images

Always:

\- Compress images  
\- Use Next.js Image  
\- Use modern formats  
\- Lazy load images

Avoid oversized assets.

\---

\# Assets

Minimize:

\- Fonts  
\- Images  
\- Icons  
\- JavaScript  
\- CSS

Load only what is required.

\---

\# Network Requests

Reduce:

\- Duplicate API Calls  
\- Waterfall Requests  
\- Unnecessary Fetches

Combine requests where appropriate.

\---

\# State Management

Store only necessary data.

Avoid:

\- Duplicate state  
\- Deep prop drilling  
\- Unnecessary global state

Keep state minimal.

\---

\# Loading Performance

Every page should:

\- Load quickly  
\- Show skeleton loaders  
\- Display meaningful loading states

Never block the UI unnecessarily.

\---

\# Dashboard Performance

Dashboards should:

\- Lazy load widgets  
\- Load data independently  
\- Avoid unnecessary refreshes  
\- Optimize charts

Never render heavy widgets simultaneously if not required.

\---

\# AI Performance

AI features should:

\- Execute efficiently  
\- Avoid unnecessary processing  
\- Reuse existing results when possible

Optimize AI workflows.

\---

\# Backend Performance

Backend should:

\- Minimize processing  
\- Use reusable services  
\- Optimize business logic  
\- Avoid duplicated calculations

Keep response times low.

\---

\# Infrastructure

Use:

\- CDN  
\- Compression  
\- HTTP Caching  
\- Optimized Assets

Reduce server workload whenever possible.

\---

\# Monitoring

Always monitor:

\- Page Load Time  
\- API Response Time  
\- Database Performance  
\- Memory Usage  
\- CPU Usage  
\- Bundle Size

Performance should be measurable.

\---

\# Code Quality

Performance should never reduce:

\- Readability  
\- Maintainability  
\- Scalability

Avoid premature optimization.

Optimize only where necessary.

\---

\# Before Completing Any Feature

Verify:

✓ Fast rendering

✓ Optimized queries

✓ Optimized API

✓ Optimized components

✓ Minimal bundle size

✓ Efficient images

✓ Proper caching

✓ Responsive UI

✓ Good Lighthouse performance

\---

\# Performance Goals

Target:

\- Fast First Load  
\- Smooth Navigation  
\- Responsive UI  
\- Efficient APIs  
\- Optimized Database  
\- Low Memory Usage  
\- Low CPU Usage

The application should feel instant.

\---

\# Forbidden Practices

Never:

\- Create N+1 Queries  
\- Use SELECT \*  
\- Load unnecessary data  
\- Render unnecessary components  
\- Fetch duplicate data  
\- Create oversized bundles  
\- Ignore lazy loading  
\- Ignore caching  
\- Ignore image optimization  
\- Ignore documentation

\---

\# Final Rule

Every implementation should improve or maintain the overall performance of the GCE platform.

Always follow the documented performance standards before modifying frontend, backend, APIs, databases, or infrastructure.

Performance is a first-class requirement, not an afterthought.  
